  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any sales-stop consequence for models above 5% (no automatic market ban), which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%, and keeps per-model rates away from the general public while giving them to purchasers. S5 sets a mandatory 8-per-100,000 recall trigger with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S3's six-year retrofit deadline and S4's 36-month suppression deadline both fall inside the acceptable ranges. S1 covers all serious incidents in 24 hours, but only confirmed minor incidents are reportable, with no explicit requirement to report during investigation."
